1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,591
Las Vegas.

2
00:00:01,951 --> 00:00:03,182
May 2008.

3
00:00:03,542 --> 00:00:05,144
A man calls 911.

4
00:00:05,484 --> 00:00:07,737
He says a masked intruder
has shot his wife.

5
00:00:08,077 --> 00:00:11,037
He says he fought the man for
the gun, got it, and shot him.

6
00:00:11,087 --> 00:00:14,047
The man he shot was Michael
Miller, a handyman he knew.

7
00:00:14,387 --> 00:00:15,827
His wife, Sharon, was dead.

8
00:00:16,187 --> 00:00:17,187
So was Miller.

9
00:00:17,305 --> 00:00:19,731
The man who made that
call was Thomas Randolph.

10
00:00:20,091 --> 00:00:21,612
Sharon was his sixth wife.

11
00:00:21,952 --> 00:00:25,766
Prosecutors alleged that Randolph
had hired Miller to kill Sharon,

12
00:00:25,766 --> 00:00:28,361
then killed Miller to
get rid of a witness.

13
00:00:28,701 --> 00:00:30,315
Randolph says he is innocent.

14
00:00:30,655 --> 00:00:32,756
He has been tried for murder three times.

15
00:00:33,096 --> 00:00:34,280
One jury acquitted him.

16
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,890
Two juries convicted him.

17
00:00:36,165 --> 00:00:40,058
And the first conviction, with its
two death sentences, was thrown out,

18
00:00:40,058 --> 00:00:43,850
because that jury had heard about
the case in which he was acquitted.

19
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:46,837
This is the true story
behind Netflix's The Widower.

20
00:00:49,777 --> 00:00:52,250
Thomas Randolph has
been married six times.

21
00:00:52,590 --> 00:00:56,607
His first marriage
lasted from 1975 to 1983.

22
00:00:56,967 --> 00:00:59,196
That wife is still alive, and she later

23
00:00:59,196 --> 00:01:01,623
testified against him
at one of his trials.

24
00:01:01,963 --> 00:01:04,784
In 1983, he married Becky Gault.

25
00:01:05,144 --> 00:01:09,463
According to reports, it was the same
day his first divorce was finalised.

26
00:01:09,803 --> 00:01:12,090
After Becky, he married four more times.

27
00:01:12,430 --> 00:01:14,195
Four of his six wives have died.

28
00:01:14,535 --> 00:01:17,797
One died in 2004, after heart surgery.

29
00:01:18,157 --> 00:01:19,551
Another died of cancer.

30
00:01:19,911 --> 00:01:21,966
He was never charged over either death.

31
00:01:22,306 --> 00:01:26,300
One, in Utah in 1986,
led to a murder trial.

32
00:01:26,660 --> 00:01:31,490
And one, in Las Vegas in 2008, led
to the sentence he is serving today.

33
00:01:31,829 --> 00:01:32,778
Utah.

34
00:01:32,828 --> 00:01:35,173
November 1986.

35
00:01:35,513 --> 00:01:39,751
Becky Gault, Randolph's second wife,
died of a gunshot wound at home.

36
00:01:40,091 --> 00:01:42,297
Her death was first ruled a suicide.

37
00:01:42,637 --> 00:01:46,198
Then a former friend and co-worker
of Randolph's, Eric Tarantino,

38
00:01:46,198 --> 00:01:48,856
told authorities that
Randolph had talked about

39
00:01:48,856 --> 00:01:51,263
having her killed for the insurance money.

40
00:01:51,603 --> 00:01:53,704
Randolph was charged with Becky's murder.

41
00:01:54,044 --> 00:01:57,788
And while he was in jail
awaiting trial, news reports say,

42
00:01:57,788 --> 00:02:01,707
he offered a cellmate cash and
a car title to kill Tarantino.

43
00:02:02,047 --> 00:02:04,508
The cellmate was an
undercover police officer.

44
00:02:04,848 --> 00:02:07,634
Randolph pleaded guilty to
felony witness tampering.

45
00:02:07,974 --> 00:02:10,631
But at the murder trial
in 1989, his lawyers

46
00:02:10,631 --> 00:02:13,129
argued that Becky had taken her own life.

47
00:02:13,469 --> 00:02:16,093
And a Utah jury acquitted him of murder.

48
00:02:16,433 --> 00:02:17,633
Remember that acquittal.

49
00:02:17,977 --> 00:02:21,785
Three decades later, in a courtroom
in Las Vegas, it would matter again.

50
00:02:22,125 --> 00:02:27,071
By 2008, Randolph was living in Las
Vegas with his sixth wife, Sharon.

51
00:02:27,411 --> 00:02:32,504
Prosecutors later said he had taken out
life insurance policies on Sharon in the

52
00:02:32,504 --> 00:02:37,361
two years before her death, and that
he stood to collect more than $300,000.

53
00:02:37,701 --> 00:02:42,279
Investigators also counted nearly 300
phone calls between Randolph and Miller in

54
00:02:42,279 --> 00:02:44,249
the months before the killings.

55
00:02:44,609 --> 00:02:46,559
Most, they said, were made by Randolph.

56
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:50,530
Randolph told police that Miller had
been wearing a mask when he shot him.

57
00:02:50,664 --> 00:02:53,261
But police said Miller had
been shot in the forehead.

58
00:02:53,311 --> 00:02:57,186
And the ski mask was found on the
garage floor, with no blood on it,

59
00:02:57,186 --> 00:02:58,547
and no bullet holes.

60
00:02:58,888 --> 00:03:00,943
Then there was the 911 call itself.

61
00:03:01,283 --> 00:03:06,275
Prosecutors said the dispatcher had to ask
Randolph several times to give Sharon CPR.

62
00:03:06,615 --> 00:03:10,477
The defence said the call captured a
man screaming and crying over his wife,

63
00:03:10,477 --> 00:03:13,302
and that he was the only
person who tried to help her.

64
00:03:13,642 --> 00:03:16,962
Detectives also recorded Randolph
walking them through the house.

65
00:03:17,322 --> 00:03:21,188
On the video, he acted out the
shootings, and, one station reported,

66
00:03:21,188 --> 00:03:23,278
mimicked the sound of the gunfire.

67
00:03:23,619 --> 00:03:25,952
Jurors at both trials
would watch that video.

68
00:03:26,292 --> 00:03:30,061
His defence argued that there was
no physical evidence of any plot,

69
00:03:30,061 --> 00:03:33,676
and that Miller acted on his own,
in a burglary that went wrong.

70
00:03:34,016 --> 00:03:37,246
In January 2009, eight
months after the shootings,

71
00:03:37,246 --> 00:03:41,400
police arrested Randolph at his
parents' home in Clearfield, Utah.

72
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:43,478
He was fifty-three.

73
00:03:43,818 --> 00:03:47,406
He was charged with conspiracy to
commit murder, and with murder.

74
00:03:47,746 --> 00:03:48,746
Then he waited.

75
00:03:48,872 --> 00:03:51,357
Almost nine years passed
before his first trial.

76
00:03:51,697 --> 00:03:55,900
In 2017, the case finally
went to trial in Las Vegas.

77
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:59,994
And this time, the jury heard
about Utah: about Becky's death,

78
00:03:59,994 --> 00:04:03,914
and witnesses who said Randolph
had tried to arrange her killing.

79
00:04:04,254 --> 00:04:06,754
Before it could be used,
the judge held a hearing.

80
00:04:06,890 --> 00:04:09,560
The State called one
witness: the prosecutor

81
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:11,696
from Randolph's Utah murder trial.

82
00:04:12,036 --> 00:04:14,706
Even though, in Utah, he had
been acquitted of her murder.

83
00:04:14,756 --> 00:04:16,857
Two of his former wives testified too.

84
00:04:17,197 --> 00:04:22,580
On the 28th of June, 2017, the jury
found Randolph guilty of conspiracy,

85
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:25,823
and of two counts of first-degree murder.

86
00:04:26,163 --> 00:04:30,610
A week later, the same jury, eight women
and four men, sentenced him to death.

87
00:04:30,970 --> 00:04:33,176
Twice: one sentence for each victim.

88
00:04:33,516 --> 00:04:34,516
He appealed.

89
00:04:34,642 --> 00:04:39,047
And on the 10th of December, 2020,
the Nevada Supreme Court threw out the

90
00:04:39,047 --> 00:04:42,839
convictions and both death sentences,
and ordered a new trial.

91
00:04:43,179 --> 00:04:46,679
The court held that the Utah evidence
should never have been admitted.

92
00:04:46,929 --> 00:04:51,503
The danger of unfair prejudice, it said,
substantially outweighed its value.

93
00:04:51,843 --> 00:04:56,023
It found that the State's proof of those
old allegations rested on one witness.

94
00:04:56,383 --> 00:04:58,683
And it noted that Randolph
had been acquitted.

95
00:04:58,743 --> 00:05:00,693
The ruling did not say he was innocent.

96
00:05:00,984 --> 00:05:02,634
It meant he would be tried again.

97
00:05:02,810 --> 00:05:07,861
In February 2021, Dateline NBC aired
a three-part series on the case,

98
00:05:07,861 --> 00:05:09,544
called The Widower.

99
00:05:09,884 --> 00:05:12,496
The retrial began in August 2023.

100
00:05:12,836 --> 00:05:16,814
This time, prosecutors were largely
limited to evidence about the deaths of

101
00:05:16,814 --> 00:05:18,386
Sharon and Michael Miller.

102
00:05:18,746 --> 00:05:20,746
And they did not seek the death penalty.

103
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:25,388
Defence attorney Josh Tomsheck argued
there was no physical evidence of a plot,

104
00:05:25,388 --> 00:05:29,593
and that Randolph was the only person
who tried to help Sharon that night.

105
00:05:29,933 --> 00:05:33,545
In August 2023, after more than
four hours of deliberation,

106
00:05:33,545 --> 00:05:37,712
the second jury found Randolph guilty
of conspiracy to commit murder,

107
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:40,602
and two counts of murder
with a deadly weapon.

108
00:05:40,942 --> 00:05:43,848
In April 2024, Judge
Tierra Jones sentenced

109
00:05:43,848 --> 00:05:46,399
him to sixty years to life in prison.

110
00:05:46,739 --> 00:05:49,107
Before he was sentenced, Randolph spoke.

111
00:05:49,447 --> 00:05:51,096
"I didn't kill Sharon," he said.

112
00:05:51,456 --> 00:05:53,106
"I have nothing to do with this."

113
00:05:53,282 --> 00:05:54,292
He appealed again.

114
00:05:54,652 --> 00:05:58,917
He argued that the years of delay had
violated his right to a speedy trial,

115
00:05:58,917 --> 00:06:02,129
and that his walkthrough
statements were not voluntary.

116
00:06:02,469 --> 00:06:08,671
On the 31st of August, 2026, the Nevada
Supreme Court rejected every argument,

117
00:06:08,671 --> 00:06:11,107
and upheld his convictions.

118
00:06:11,447 --> 00:06:15,447
The court said the nine years before his
first trial did not violate his rights.

119
00:06:15,801 --> 00:06:19,245
The nineteen months before his retrial
were long enough to be presumed

120
00:06:19,245 --> 00:06:21,919
prejudicial, it said, but
the State was not to blame.

121
00:06:22,259 --> 00:06:27,182
He had also argued that he was in pain and
on medication when he spoke to detectives.

122
00:06:27,542 --> 00:06:30,011
Two detectives testified
otherwise, and the

123
00:06:30,011 --> 00:06:32,429
court refused to throw out his statements.

124
00:06:32,769 --> 00:06:35,265
Today, Randolph is in his seventies.

125
00:06:35,625 --> 00:06:39,143
He is serving his sentence at Lovelock
Correctional Center, in Nevada.

126
00:06:39,483 --> 00:06:41,399
He has said he is innocent.

127
00:06:41,739 --> 00:06:46,471
Dateline producer Dan Slepian had been
embedded with Las Vegas police in 2008,

128
00:06:46,471 --> 00:06:48,612
and followed the case for years.

129
00:06:48,952 --> 00:06:53,665
On the 30th of September, 2026,
Netflix released The Widower:

130
00:06:53,665 --> 00:06:57,393
'Til Death Do Us Part,
directed by Chris Smith.

131
00:06:57,733 --> 00:07:01,796
It follows Slepian and Las Vegas
police detective Dean O'Kelley.

132
00:07:02,136 --> 00:07:05,394
In its first week,
it drew 11.6 million views,

133
00:07:05,394 --> 00:07:10,344
and was reported as Netflix's number-two
English-language film worldwide.

134
00:07:10,684 --> 00:07:12,484
So here is where the record stands.

135
00:07:12,824 --> 00:07:17,259
In Utah, a jury acquitted Randolph
of murder in Becky Gault's death.

136
00:07:17,619 --> 00:07:19,569
He pleaded guilty to witness tampering.

137
00:07:19,898 --> 00:07:22,998
No charge was ever brought over
the deaths of two other wives.

138
00:07:23,291 --> 00:07:25,469
And in Las Vegas, two juries convicted him

139
00:07:25,469 --> 00:07:27,784
over the deaths of Sharon
and Michael Miller.

140
00:07:28,144 --> 00:07:29,794
The first verdict was overturned.

141
00:07:30,106 --> 00:07:31,546
The second has been upheld.

142
00:07:31,886 --> 00:07:33,500
Randolph says he is innocent.
